+# Closed legacy Focus CPU source transition
+
+The native ExecutionProfile owner may retain the original public Focus profile
+04821eda only in an exact pre-1.9 native release series. The new private witness
+is not deserializable and does not grant model, lease, source-read, reservation
+or execution authority. Existing release/local-candidate and EvaluationOwner
+admission, consent, hardware fit, same-worker leases and original deadlines remain.
+
+The row binds the complete canonical Rust Profile value SHA73d884fb1c2b37709d4d1b1daa93fd65687ce310cbd4096af0ef106a615e608c
+and its unique immutable native catalog member, including every graph/external
+weight/tokenizer/compiler/CAL/notice/fixture identity, byte length, ABI, CpuFit,
+resource/token/candidate limits, task, qualification and public URL. Actual native
+Scorer/AssetSource still authenticate physical asset bytes. Existing bytes/URLs
+are never rewritten. GPU execution descriptors and both Context profiles refuse.
+
+Exact source mapping: legacy Focus Core ddd9dbc7.../task cfbcbe4c... to current
+Focus Core77fa25e4.../task5add2b52..., with compiler.rs09c3120d... and
+compiler/focus.rs66f9231b... unchanged. Current source mismatches refuse; future
+source updates require a newly reviewed row, not broad prefix compatibility.
+The changed Core runtime predicate accepts exactly the same CPU literal and adds
+strict device identities on separate paths; CPU ranking/window/ordering/scoring
+constraints and compiler arrays/quoting/readout are retained. The new /2 empty
+Context calibration has no effect on Focus. No public Context1271 compatibility
+or private8192Compact admission/promotion is inferred.
+
+Native runtime integration must retain this witness inside ExecutionProfile and
+repeat it at from_release, release_asset_profile, EvaluationCatalog construction
+and lookup, and Scorer admission, replacing duplicated Focus policy equality only
+for this exact closed CPU row. Current policies remain the default; no unchecked
+Profile-shaped JSON value acquires a capability. Compilation and actual native
+CPU refusal/recovery tests precede activation.
+
+The existing current Rust Compiler still creates NEW source-bound input digests.
+The native owner records each such digest with a separate source-transition
+record/binding immediately after compilation; it never relabels old numeric/CAL
+evidence as current. This record is private native execution provenance, no new
+public DTO or qualification. Actual native image/build/source receipts remain
+separate and must be retained. Original CPU Profile serialization and advice
+runtime literal remain unchanged. No CPU-as-GPU label or old proof transfer.
+
+The row binds exact legacy runtime source d2879546ba9e949fdd8b135a244923de2adb781e8598539cc33f4d7d6f0794eb
+to reviewed proposed runtime hook source9e539508f52e403368124ee38f91085f4b318f87fcffe45f898728cf9c0db49d.
+The native module rehashes its compiled runtime source; mismatches refuse. Source
+review, combined compilation and native controls remain pending; none is claimed
+from private preparation. Future runtime/source changes need a new exact row,
+never arbitrary stale-policy fallback.
+
+## Reviewed G5 CPU/F32 source supplement
+
+The predecessor source mapping to9e539508... remains historical. The new exact current runtime source is dde0c85f555f5101a17c0035186fdafc854bab14793f08abc198c009f5424e1d. The old parent9e is not accepted in place of currentdde by this build. This is one closed current-source row, never a prefix/list/any-CPU exception.
+
+The complete declared runtime delta was inverted to byte-equal normalized9e as retained in the private preparation receipt. CPU/F32 execution keeps original validatedgraph/external1-F32/2-U8 loader, CPUprovider, compiler/token arrays/output ABI/rawhead, CPUfit/reservations, and score paths. NewF16plan is None on CPU/F32; type10 loading, G5 metadata/math/mask/backend checks execute only with actualF16CUDA binding. F32 CUDA keeps its exact prior provider/math /1 and consuming typed strict placement. The central initialization observes inherited tuning settings but does not set/reject/change CPU/F32 math.
+
+All complete legacy Profile73d884/public04821/compiler2cba/CALc458/assets/URLs/versionless-than1.9 and source admission checks remain. The record schema/frame dimensions remain /1; current_runtime_source and transition_source change, so its row/newinput binding changes. Old native rows/receipts/numeric/CAL/resource/task verdicts stay historical and are never rewritten or qualified. The existing witness repeats current-source checks at every admission/use; no decodeddescriptor permits execution.
